statement:
Let \(n,d\in\mathbb Z_{>0}\), let \(C\subseteq\mathbb R^n\times\mathbb R^d\) be a convex body of positive mixed volume, and put \(C_z=\{x:(z,x)\in C\}\), \(a_z=\operatorname{vol}_d(C_z)\), \(Z=\{z\in\mathbb Z^n:a_z>0\}\), and \(W=\sum_z a_z\). The support \(Z\) includes all actual positive-volume integer fibers. Set \(\gamma_d=(d/(d+1))^d\), \(c_z=a_z^{-1}\int_{C_z}x\,dx\), \(\mathcal K_z=\mathsf M_{a_z/2}(C_z)\), and \(D_z=\mathcal K_z-c_z\).

Retain one common canonical zero-fresh hard system of accepted facts 4ebcf4455419a224 and dcca4b6d66d80dd4, together with its original reservoir and hard ledger from c81f02314cb34f8b and 637b5f7874d8c875. Thus \(r\) remains the original half-strength product reservoir, \(Q=|r|>0\), \(G\) remains the original global complete metronoid-core capacity, and \(D=2^nh_{\max}(C)\) remains the original scaled depth. In particular \(G+D<Q/100\). No continuous body \(D_z\) is identified with the scalar \(D\).

Fix any allowed synchronous first-label parameters. For a positive first label \(\tau=(\alpha,j,i,k)\), the exact aliases to dcca4b6d66d80dd4 and 4ebcf4455419a224 are
\[
\zeta_\tau=m_j,\qquad
w_\tau^{(1)}=\frac{q_j^\alpha\pi_i^\alpha\pi_k^\alpha}{2},\qquad
y_\tau=y_{\alpha,j,i,k},\qquad
x_\tau^\pm=x_{\alpha,j,i,k}^\pm,\qquad
z_\tau^\pm=z_j^\pm.
\]
Thus \(y_\tau=(x_\tau^-+x_\tau^+)/2\), with \(x_\tau^\pm\in\mathcal K_{z_\tau^\pm}\). Define
\[
t_u=\sum_{\tau:\zeta_\tau=u}w_\tau^{(1)}=\frac{\eta_u}{2},\qquad
T_1=\sum_u t_u=\frac{\Omega_b}{2}>\frac{97Q}{200},\qquad
T_\xi=\sum_{u\equiv\xi}t_u.
\tag{1}
\]
Unused targets have mass zero. The original target packing gives \(t_u\le a_u/2\). For a nonempty current target class, set \(M_\xi^t=\max_{u\equiv\xi}t_u\), and call it current good when \(M_\xi^t\le T_\xi/4\). Let \(\mathscr G_t\) be the set of these classes and \(T_g=\sum_{\xi\in\mathscr G_t}T_\xi\). This goodness is recomputed from \(t\); it is distinct from original-volume goodness in the definition of \(r\). Empty classes have no denominator and contribute zero.

For unordered distinct physical targets define
\[
q_{\{u,v\}}^{\mathrm{new}}
=\frac{2\gamma_dt_ut_v}{T_\xi}
\quad(u<v,\ u\equiv v\equiv\xi,\ \xi\in\mathscr G_t),
\qquad q_e^{\mathrm{new}}=0\text{ otherwise},\qquad
B_{\mathrm{new}}=|q^{\mathrm{new}}|.
\tag{2}
\]
Here \(u<v\) is any fixed total order. The following exact capacities and linear bounds hold:
\[
\begin{aligned}
d_u(q^{\mathrm{new}})
&=2\gamma_dt_u\left(1-\frac{t_u}{T_\xi}\right)
\le 2\gamma_dt_u\le\gamma_da_u\le\frac{a_u}{2}
&&\text{in a current good class},\\
T_g&\ge T_1-2G,\\
B_{\mathrm{new}}
&=\gamma_dT_g-F_{\mathrm{phys}}^{\mathrm{new}},\qquad
F_{\mathrm{phys}}^{\mathrm{new}}
=\gamma_d\sum_{\xi\in\mathscr G_t}
\frac{\sum_{u\equiv\xi}t_u^2}{T_\xi}
\le\frac{\gamma_dG}{2},\\
B_{\mathrm{new}}
&\ge\max\left\{\frac{3\gamma_dT_g}{4},
\gamma_d\left(T_1-\frac{5G}{2}\right)\right\}>0.
\end{aligned}
\tag{3}
\]
Degrees are zero outside current good classes. The physical diagonal in (3) includes all pairs of first labels with equal physical target, including distinct labels with that target. It is not the circuit-coordinate diagonal of dcca4b6d66d80dd4.

Use the global capacity \(\mathfrak M_{\mathrm{aff}}(C)\) in exactly the normalization of accepted fact 8c92d1d2b1a1b7f5. Then
\[
R_C(q^{\mathrm{new}})\le\mathfrak M_{\mathrm{aff}}(C)
\le\frac D{\gamma_d}.
\tag{4}
\]
Apply accepted fact 6496cb3b0fd44f9d afresh with the exact aliases
\(q\mapsto q^{\mathrm{new}}\), \(Q\mapsto B_{\mathrm{new}}\), \(v_e\mapsto v_e^{\mathrm{new}}\), \(\omega_e\mapsto\omega_e^{\mathrm{new}}\), and \(\Omega\mapsto\Omega_{\mathrm{new}}\). Its original pair bodies retain their meanings:
\(m_e=(u+v)/2\), \(L_e=(\mathcal K_u+\mathcal K_v)/2\), and \(D_e=(D_u+D_v)/2\). The actual load-minimal fresh optimizer satisfies
\[
0\le\omega_e^{\mathrm{new}}\le q_e^{\mathrm{new}},\qquad
\Omega_{\mathrm{new}}
\ge B_{\mathrm{new}}-\frac D{\gamma_d}
\ge\gamma_d\left(T_1-\frac{5G}{2}\right)-\frac D{\gamma_d}
>\frac{79Q}{600}.
\tag{5}
\]
For its actual contacts \(\ell_e^{\mathrm{new}}\in L_e\), the measure
\[
\sigma_{\mathrm{new}}^{\mathrm{fresh}}
=\frac12\sum_e\omega_e^{\mathrm{new}}
\delta_{(m_e,\ell_e^{\mathrm{new}})}
\tag{6}
\]
is carried by \(S=C\cap(\mathbb Z^n\times\mathbb R^d)\), has mass greater than \(79Q/1200\), and is dominated by the original mixed-volume measure \(\mu_C\) on every closed ambient halfspace. Equations (4)-(5) use the global affine matching capacity, not monotonicity relative to \(r\). No inequality \(q^{\mathrm{new}}\le r\) is asserted or used.

Separately, for first labels at distinct targets \(u<v\) in a current good class, set
\[
\alpha_{\tau\sigma}^{\mathrm{new}}
=\frac{2\gamma_dw_\tau^{(1)}w_\sigma^{(1)}}{T_\xi},\qquad
Y_{\tau\sigma}^{\mathrm{new}}
=\frac{y_\tau+y_\sigma}{2}
=\frac{x_\tau^-+x_\tau^++x_\sigma^-+x_\sigma^+}{4}.
\tag{7}
\]
For incidence identities, extend \(\alpha_{\tau\sigma}^{\mathrm{new}}\) symmetrically when the physical order is reversed. Every atom sum below counts the unordered physical pair once. Put
\(N_z(\tau)=\mathbf1_{\{z_\tau^-=z\}}+\mathbf1_{\{z_\tau^+=z\}}\). The exact full-occurrence charge is
\[
\begin{aligned}
L_z^{\mathrm{new}}
&=\sum_{\tau,\sigma}\alpha_{\tau\sigma}^{\mathrm{new}}
\bigl(N_z(\tau)+N_z(\sigma)\bigr)\\
&=\sum_{\xi\in\mathscr G_t}\sum_{\tau:\zeta_\tau\equiv\xi}
2\gamma_dw_\tau^{(1)}
\left(1-\frac{t_{\zeta_\tau}}{T_\xi}\right)N_z(\tau)
\le\gamma_d\beta_z\le\frac{\gamma_da_z}{4}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{8}
\]
The \(\beta_z\) here is exactly the original source budget of dcca4b6d66d80dd4. Every original occurrence, including a repeated leaf in one atom, is charged at its full \(\alpha_{\tau\sigma}^{\mathrm{new}}\)-weight. There is no discount by its barycentric coefficient \(1/4\). Consequently
\[
\sigma_{\mathrm{new}}^{\mathrm{anc}}
=2\sum_{\tau,\sigma}\alpha_{\tau\sigma}^{\mathrm{new}}
\delta_{((\zeta_\tau+\zeta_\sigma)/2,Y_{\tau\sigma}^{\mathrm{new}})}
\tag{9}
\]
is carried by \(S\), has mass \(2B_{\mathrm{new}}\), and is dominated by \(\mu_C\) on every closed ambient halfspace, including boundary atoms. The measures (6) and (9) are separate certificates. Their points are not identified, and their domination bounds are not added.

The following exact arithmetic audit also holds. For \(\xi\in\mathscr G_t\), let
\(\mu_\xi=T_\xi^{-1}\sum_{u\equiv\xi}t_uu\) and
\(V_\xi=\sum_{u\equiv\xi}t_u\|u-\mu_\xi\|^2\), using the Euclidean norm on the base. For every \(p\in\mathbb R^n\),
\[
\begin{aligned}
I(q^{\mathrm{new}};p)
&:=\sum_eq_e^{\mathrm{new}}\|m_e-p\|^2\\
&=\gamma_d\sum_{\xi\in\mathscr G_t}
\left(T_\xi\|\mu_\xi-p\|^2+\frac{V_\xi}{2}
-\frac1{T_\xi}\sum_{u\equiv\xi}t_u^2\|u-p\|^2\right).
\end{aligned}
\tag{10}
\]
Write \(\kappa_e=q_e^{\mathrm{new}}-\omega_e^{\mathrm{new}}\). Then
\(\delta:=\sum_e\kappa_e=B_{\mathrm{new}}-\Omega_{\mathrm{new}}\le D/\gamma_d\). The proposed pooled fresh masses are
\(t'_m=\frac12\sum_{e:m_e=m}\omega_e^{\mathrm{new}}\), with total mass \(T'=\Omega_{\mathrm{new}}/2\). For each nonempty new physical parity class \(\eta\), put \(T'_\eta=\sum_{m\equiv\eta}t'_m\) and \(\mu'_\eta=(T'_\eta)^{-1}\sum_{m\equiv\eta}t'_mm\). Its parity-conditioned spread obeys the exact identity
\[
\Phi(t'):=\sum_\eta\sum_{m\equiv\eta}t'_m\|m-\mu'_\eta\|^2
=\frac12 I(q^{\mathrm{new}};p)
-\frac12\sum_e\kappa_e\|m_e-p\|^2
-\sum_\eta T'_\eta\|\mu'_\eta-p\|^2.
\tag{11}
\]
The new parity classes can mix different old class means. The removed mass bound alone controls neither the removed first moment nor the removed second moment without a bound on the base locations.

There is a finite decreasing support potential. For any nonempty finite current base support \(A\subseteq\mathbb Z^n\), define
\(N(A)=|\operatorname{conv}(A)\cap\mathbb Z^n|\). If a nonempty next support consists of midpoints of distinct elements of \(A\), then its \(N\) is strictly smaller. This applies to the actual positive fresh support in (6), and to the positive ancestral support in (9).

These arithmetic facts leave the descent unresolved. In particular, the proposed fresh masses satisfy
\[
T'=\frac{\Omega_{\mathrm{new}}}{2}
\le\frac{B_{\mathrm{new}}}{2}
\le\frac{\gamma_dT_1}{2}\le\frac{T_1}{4}.
\tag{12}
\]
The conclusions above do not establish one joint fresh target density family with pointwise bound \(\frac12\mathbf1_{C_m}\), do not establish \(t'_m\le a_m/2\) for every physical target, and do not establish an absolute mass floor through an arbitrary number of steps. Thus the integer support descent does not close the locked conjecture.
